<!-- 5. WHAT RADAR WATCHES -->
<section class="section" id="radar-watches">
 <div class="container">
  <header class="sec-head reveal">
   <span class="kicker">What Radar Watches</span>
   <h2>See your brand <span class="grad gradline">the way the market sees it.</span></h2>
  </header>
  <div class="r-grid r-grid--3 reveal">
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Market Presence</h4><h3>Are people talking about you?</h3><p>Radar tracks where your brand and competitors appear across relevant publishers, customer conversations, communities, search results, AI answers, marketplaces, and other external sources. See who's getting the attention, where, and how your share of the conversation is changing.</p></div>
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Message Ownership</h4><h3>Are competitors selling your story better than you are?</h3><p>Radar compares what your brand says with what competitors say, and what customers and the market actually associate with each brand. If you have the stronger warranty, feature, proof point, or benefit but a competitor communicates it more effectively, Radar is designed to find that gap.</p></div>
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Advertising Intelligence</h4><h3>Are you being out-advertised, or out-messaged?</h3><p>Radar compares competitor advertising activity, creative velocity, offers, hooks, formats, products, and messaging against your own. It looks for the difference that matters: Are they testing faster? Using a stronger hook or an offer you're not? Emphasizing a problem you could credibly own?</p></div>
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Search &amp; AI Visibility</h4><h3>Where does AI recommend you, and where are you invisible?</h3><p>Radar monitors how your brand and competitors appear across search engines, AI answer engines, and other discovery environments. When competitors appear and you don't, Radar looks deeper: which sources influence the answer, what content earns visibility, and what could help close the gap.</p></div>
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Customer &amp; Market Movement</h4><h3>What is your customer starting to care about?</h3><p>Radar looks for meaningful changes in customer questions, problems, language, reviews, use cases, and buying criteria, and identifies which brands are best positioned to benefit.</p></div>
   <div class="r-card"><h4>Market &amp; Platform Changes</h4><h3>What changed that could affect your business?</h3><p>Meta. Google. Amazon. AI shopping. Marketplaces. Shipping. Regulation. Technology. Radar filters out the noise and focuses on the question that matters: what changed that affects your business, and what, if anything, should you do about it?</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="r-actions reveal" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:30px">
   <a href="#radar-waitlist" class="btn btn--solid btn--lg">Join the Radar Waitlist</a>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

